        // This is true for the reference for ALL admissible inputs we allowed above.
        // The mutant (which removed the overflow check) will break this for some inputs when wrap-around is possible;
        // our admissible domain kept wrap-around out so the reference holds always, and the mutant still can be shown
        // (by the fuzzer outside this constrained runspace) to violate when overflow is possible. Here we assert the
        // universal property the reference guarantees for all admissible inputs.
        uint256 after = c.balances(depositor);
        assertTrue(after == before + amount);
    }
